<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Áed mac Ainmuirech</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 598</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Áed mac Ainmuirech was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenél Conaill</a> of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> and high king of Ireland in the late sixth century. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adomnan">Adomnán</a> he met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> in the presence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/convention-of-druim-cett">Convention of Druim Cett</a>. He was killed in 598 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dun-bolg">Battle of Dún Bolg</a> in Leinster.</p></div>
